# cPanel api/ rsync filters (use: rsync --filter='merge scripts/cpanel-rsync-api.filters')
#
# P .env       never delete the server's .env when using --delete
# - .env       never copy a .env from the CI checkout (secrets live only on the server)
# - writable   runtime state (logs, cache, migration run logs) belongs to the server
# - tests      not needed at runtime
#
# .env.example IS deployed from git on every release.

# .env.example must survive the workflow's --exclude='.env.*', which otherwise strips it and
# leaves a first deploy with nothing to bootstrap .env from. Merge-file rules are evaluated
# before the command-line excludes, so this include wins.
+ .env.example
P .env
- .env
P writable/logs/**
P writable/cache/**
P writable/session/**
P writable/debugbar/**
P writable/migration/**
- writable/logs/**
- writable/cache/**
- writable/session/**
- writable/debugbar/**
- writable/migration/**
- tests/
- .phpunit.result.cache
- phpunit.xml
- phpunit-integration.xml
- .gitignore
